      "comment": "Zaha Hadi: Faranak",
      "content": "Zaha Hadi remembers Faranak as a young, golden-haired student who sat in the first row, was admired by many and worked with a frown and a hand on her forehead. Faranak once said that true art cannot be understood, though an artist wishes someone would. Zaha thinks the heartbreak of genius is finding someone who understands their ideas.\n\nZaha suggests Faranak chose her husband, who could not understand her designs, because he stayed beside her. Kaveh uses this to guess that the notebook's password is companionship.",
